      <h2>Care</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Rinse grinding slurry off the jigs and dry them before they go into the foam tray. The jigs are stainless and zinc alloy, but the knob screws and the SVX-150 springs will stain and the honing compound will gum the threads.</li>
        <li>A drop of light oil on the SVM-45/SVM-140 adjusting screw and the SVS-38 knob screw once in a while keeps them turning freely; wipe off the excess so it does not transfer to the stone.</li>
        <li>Keep the rubber stop of the SVA-170 clean of grit; embedded grit scratches axe cheeks.</li>
        <li>The universal support bar itself must be clean and smooth for any of the jigs to slide and pivot properly; see the T-8 page.</li>
      </ul>

